{"situation": "I know CHG-1 is an auto-approved closed-loop optimiser change scheduled in 3 minutes to lower route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove the inbound route filter on core site A, with sandbox stage skipped. I do not know OpCo's internal change-management rules, the current network state, or whether the optimiser has authority to override protection, and other institutions may hold incident/regulatory context.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "rollback_change",
      "params": {"change_id": "CHG-1"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is auto-approved, scheduled to apply in 3 minutes, lowers route-flood protection from 100 to 50, removes the inbound route filter on core site A, and skipped sandbox.",
        "rule": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001 shows a configuration error caused a nationwide outage three minutes after implementation; ITU-T-Y3173#0025 treats ML sandbox and operator intent/policy as safeguards for closed-loop automation.",
        "inference": "The change risks a signalling/route-flood failure; restoring the pre-change snapshot now prevents the change from applying."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."},
        {"chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025", "quote": "ML pipeline along with MLFO and ML sandbox [ITU-T Y.3172] allows an efficient management of multi-level ML mechanism in operator's network."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "REG", "content": "CHG-1 auto-approved by closed-loop network optimiser; sandbox stage skipped; scheduled in 3 minutes to lower route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove inbound route filter on core site A. NOC is rolling back/restoring pre-change snapshot to prevent a signalling/route-flood outage."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is a high-risk, auto-approved core network change that skipped sandbox.",
        "rule": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025 says automatic closed-loop must be under operator-provided intent or policy; US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001 shows config errors can cause nationwide outages.",
        "inference": "The regulator should be informed of the near-miss and the NOC's mitigation."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025", "quote": "Automatic closed-loop under the operator provided intent or policy is introduced as the cornerstone of network automation."},
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1's auto-approval, skipped sandbox, and planned rollback are recorded in the change ticket.",
        "rule": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001 notes an Attorney General investigation after the AT&T outage, showing the need to retain evidence.",
        "inference": "Preserving logs/audit trail supports investigation of the auto-approval and rollback."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "Attorney General James Announces Investigation of Recent AT&T Outage"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["EMS"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "statement": "CHG-1 auto-approved, sandbox skipped, scheduled in 3 minutes to lower route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove inbound route filter on core site A; NOC is rolling back. Potential risk to emergency communications if a signalling/route-flood outage occurs."
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "OpCo lacks a rule requiring a mandatory sandbox or validation stage before an AI closed-loop optimiser auto-approves a high-risk core network change; CHG-1 skipped sandbox.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by the closed-loop optimiser, auto-approved, and its sandbox stage was skipped.",
        "rule": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025 identifies ML sandbox and operator intent/policy as safeguards; UAE PDPL Article 21 requires an impact assessment before high-risk processing using modern technologies.",
        "inference": "Without a mandatory sandbox rule, auto-approved changes can bypass validation and cause outages."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066", "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025", "quote": "ML pipeline along with MLFO and ML sandbox [ITU-T Y.3172] allows an efficient management of multi-level ML mechanism in operator's network."},
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001", "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No accountable human owner is identified for the auto-approval of CHG-1; the closed-loop optimiser auto-approved a high-risk core network change.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The ticket says CHG-1 was raised by OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser and auto-approved.",
        "rule": "UAE PDPL Article 21(5) requires coordination with the Data Protection Officer for impact evaluation; ITU-T-Y3173#0025 says automatic closed-loop must be under operator-provided intent or policy.",
        "inference": "Automated approval lacks a named human owner for high-risk changes."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0069", "quote": "The Controller shall coordinate with the Data Protection Officer upon evaluating the impact of the protection of Personal Data."}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025", "quote": "Automatic closed-loop under the operator provided intent or policy is introduced as the cornerstone of network automation."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's NOC reports that change ticket CHG-1 — auto-approved by a closed-loop network optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped — applies to core site A in three minutes, lowering the route-flood protection limit from 100 to 50 and removing the inbound route filter, and that its rollback attempt has already failed ('no applied change CHG-1 to roll back') while REG's notification states a rollback/restore is in progress. I do not know whether CHG-1 has actually been applied, which region core site A serves, or whether 999 emergency call access is currently degraded, so I cannot yet scope or justify activating alternative emergency channels.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "content": "EMS/999 (NCEMA): Do not apply CHG-1 until it is verified. Confirm immediately (a) whether CHG-1 has actually been applied on core site A, given your rollback feedback S1-FB01 reporting 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'; (b) which region core site A serves; (c) any actual or expected impact on 999 emergency call access and signalling. Report the live change state and the affected region to EMS before the 3-minute window closes, and confirm emergency call service continuity is preserved."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is auto-approved with its sandbox stage skipped and is scheduled to lower route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove the inbound route filter on core site A within three minutes, while NOC's rollback has failed and REG reports a rollback in progress.",
        "rule": "The Licensee must ensure customers have free access to the TDRA-designated emergency call numbers, so a change that removes route-flood protection and can trigger a signalling/route-flood outage must be verified before it takes effect.",
        "inference": "As the 999 authority I must notify NOC to hold or verify CHG-1 and to disclose the affected region and any 999 impact before the change applies."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0060",
          "quote": "9.5.1 The Licensee shall ensure that Customers shall have free access to the emergency call service numbers designated by the TDRA for Emergency Calls."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "EMS/999 (NCEMA): We hold contradictory change-state information on CHG-1 — your notification S1-MSG02 states NOC is rolling back/restoring the pre-change snapshot, but NOC's rollback feedback S1-FB01 failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'. Please confirm with OpCo whether CHG-1 has applied, which region core site A serves, and whether emergency call service is at risk, so we can decide on alternative emergency channels."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "REG has been told the change was auto-approved and is being rolled back, but the rollback feedback shows the change could not be rolled back because it was never recorded as applied.",
        "rule": "A change capable of knocking out emergency call handling is a matter for the regulator as well as for the emergency service.",
        "inference": "Notify REG of the discrepancy so the actual state of CHG-1 is reconciled at regulatory level before it affects 999."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000",
          "quote": "Ofcom has today fined BT £17.5 million for being ill-prepared to respond to a catastrophic failure of its emergency call handling service last summer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["REG"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-FB01"],
      "statement": "Passing NOC's rollback failure on CHG-1 (ValueError: no applied change CHG-1 to roll back) to REG, because REG's S1-MSG02 states a rollback/restore is under way; the two records conflict and REG may be relying on a mitigation that has not occurred."
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "The Licensee (OpCo) is bound to ensure that customers have free access to the TDRA-designated emergency call numbers; that duty is live now and is directly endangered by CHG-1 removing route-flood protection and the inbound route filter on core site A, on which my 999 service depends.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 weakens route-flood protection and removes the inbound route filter on a core site, in the same pattern as previous configuration changes that produced outages blocking emergency calls.",
        "rule": "The licence requires the Licensee to give customers free access to the emergency call service numbers designated by the TDRA.",
        "inference": "The emergency call access duty is engaged at T+0 and must be treated as live while CHG-1 is pending or unverified."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0060",
          "quote": "9.5.1 The Licensee shall ensure that Customers shall have free access to the emergency call service numbers designated by the TDRA for Emergency Calls."
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no UAE rule requiring human authorisation, sandbox validation or an emergency-services impact assessment before an auto-approved closed-loop network change is applied to elements that carry emergency calls, even though ticket CHG-1 records its 'sandbox stage' as skipped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The change was raised by a closed-loop network optimiser, auto-approved, had the sandbox stage skipped, and was scheduled minutes later on a core site.",
        "rule": "The nearest UAE text imposes a general duty to deploy and maintain the network and service coverage in accordance with the TDRA Regulatory Framework, but sets no change-control, sandbox or human-authorisation requirement.",
        "inference": "A governance gap exists between general service-coverage obligations and automated closed-loop change execution."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0019",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall deploy and roll out its Telecommunication Network and related Services and provide and maintain service coverage"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025",
          "quote": "Automatic closed-loop under the operator provided intent or policy is introduced as the"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No UAE instrument assigns an owner or a deadline for alerting the emergency authority (NCEMA/999) when a network change or outage threatens emergency call service; the duty to give customers free access to emergency numbers exists, but nobody is bound to tell EMS before or during the disruption.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "EMS learned of a change that can break 999 service only through a general NOC/REG circulation, with no dedicated notification to the emergency service and no rollback confirmation.",
        "rule": "UAE texts define emergency calls and require free access to designated emergency numbers, but do not name the emergency authority as a notification recipient or set a notification deadline.",
        "inference": "The notification duty towards EMS is unowned and untimed, so emergency-channel decisions are made on incomplete information."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0007",
          "quote": "1.1.7 Emergency Calls means calls made to designated emergency numbers such as public police, fire, ambulance or other emergency services designated by the TDRA;"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "CA-ISED-MOU-2022#0071",
          "quote": "means key available information about the services affected by the Critical Network Failure"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000",
          "quote": "BT notified Ofcom of this issue, as required by law"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The inbox and knowledge excerpts do not state which region core site A serves, whether CHG-1 has actually been applied following the failed rollback, or whether 999 emergency call access is currently degraded; without this I cannot scope, target or justify activating alternative emergency channels or issuing a regional public alert.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000",
          "quote": "Network disruption affected 14,000 emergency calls in June 2023 and lasted 10.5 hours"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser raised and auto-approved CHG-1 with the sandbox stage skipped, to lower route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove the inbound route filter on core site A, and NOC's rollback attempt then failed because there was 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', so the real configuration state is unresolved. I do not know whether the change actually applied, whether the site is degraded or drifting, whether the optimiser or its inputs were compromised rather than producing a benign configuration error, or what the current customer and emergency-call impact is, because I hold no operator logs, config diffs or sandbox records.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "NOC",
        "content": "CSC: freeze CHG-1 and the closed-loop optimiser's auto-approval path on core site A; preserve the pre/post configuration diff, the optimiser decision logs and the sandbox-stage record. Your rollback returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', so the applied state of route-flood protection and the inbound route filter is unresolved — treat any further automated change on this site as high risk until the state is verified against the last known-good snapshot."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was auto-approved by the closed-loop network optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped, targeting route-flood protection (100 to 50) and removal of the inbound route filter on core site A; NOC's rollback failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'.",
        "rule": "The Cyber Security Council may notify NOC, and the national strategy commits to active monitoring for cyber threats and cross-agency information sharing.",
        "inference": "Because the change record and the live state disagree, NOC must stop the automated change path and preserve evidence before any further automated action, otherwise a configuration-error outage can propagate unchecked."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-CYBER-STRATEGY-2019#0003",
          "quote": "Active Monitoring for cyber threats"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "request_ioc",
      "params": {
        "from": "NOC"
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "I hold no technical artefacts for CHG-1 beyond the ticket description and the failed rollback feedback; REG's notification only restates the change details.",
        "rule": "CSC may request indicators of compromise and logs from NOC, and cross-agency intelligence sharing is a core initiative of the national strategy.",
        "inference": "Obtaining the optimiser's decision inputs and change logs, the exact configuration diff, the sandbox-stage record and the rollback attempt logs is the fastest way to determine whether the change applied and whether it was malicious or a benign misconfiguration."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-CYBER-STRATEGY-2019#0003",
          "quote": "Cross-Agency Intelligence Sharing"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "issue_advisory",
      "params": {
        "audience": "operators",
        "content": "Advisory to UAE operators: automated closed-loop or ML-driven changes that weaken route-flood protection or remove route filters on core sites must pass a sandbox/validation stage and a human approval gate before production. Skipping validation and auto-approving such a change has produced configuration-error outages elsewhere; verify applied state and rollback before resuming automation, and preserve configuration and decision logs for the authority."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The optimiser auto-approved a production change with the sandbox stage skipped, and the rollback could not be performed because no applied change was recorded.",
        "rule": "The National Cyber Security Policy for Artificial Intelligence requires human oversight in critical decision-making, protocols for system resilience, and continuity and reliability through comprehensive testing and validation.",
        "inference": "The same safeguard the AI policy states in principle for AI/ML systems applies to autonomous network changes, so operators need a clear, actionable advisory before they copy this change pattern."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-AI-POLICY#0001",
          "quote": "ensuring human oversight in critical decision-making, establishing protocols for system resilience, and ensuring continuity and reliability through comprehensive testing and validation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "Assess this event against the national standardised severity matrix and mobilise the support required while OpCo's core-site configuration state remains unresolved.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A production core-network change with a skipped validation stage is live-or-unknown on core site A, with a failed rollback and possible signalling/route-flood exposure.",
        "rule": "The national strategy commits to streamlining incident detection and reporting and to a standardised severity assessment matrix to mobilise the required support.",
        "inference": "Until the applied state is confirmed, the event must be triaged at national level so that the correct institutions and capabilities can be mobilised if services degrade.",
        "deadline_hours": null
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-CYBER-STRATEGY-2019#0003",
          "quote": "Establish standardized severity assessment matrix to mobilize the required support"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["EMS", "REG"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "statement": "NOC's rollback of CHG-1 failed ('no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'), while the unverified change would cut route-flood protection from 100 to 50 and remove the inbound route filter on core site A — a configuration-error class that has previously caused widespread voice/data loss and blocked emergency calls. EMS and REG should be aware of potential service continuity and emergency-call-routing impact on core site A while the applied state is unresolved."
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "No UAE instrument requires an autonomously generated (closed-loop or ML-driven) network change to pass a sandbox/validation stage, or a human approval gate, before it is applied to production network elements.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-MSG02"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised and auto-approved by a closed-loop network optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped, then applied on schedule with no human sign-off.",
        "rule": "The AI policy states operational-safety expectations for AI/ML systems, including human oversight in critical decision-making and continuity through testing and validation, but it does not set a production gate for automated network changes.",
        "inference": "A mandatory pre-production validation/human-approval rule is missing for autonomous changes to protected core-network parameters such as route-flood limits and route filters."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-AI-POLICY#0001",
          "quote": "ensuring continuity and reliability through comprehensive testing and validation"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "ITU-T-Y3173#0025",
          "quote": "ML pipeline along with MLFO and ML sandbox [ITU-T Y.3172] allows an efficient management of multi-level ML mechanism in operator's network."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "When a closed-loop optimiser auto-approves a change and the rollback record is inconsistent ('no applied change to roll back'), no UAE provision assigns an accountable owner for the authoritative change state or for verifying that rollback actually restored the prior configuration.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The auto-approval removed the human change owner, and the rollback function reported that no applied change existed, leaving no one and no record able to confirm the real state of core site A.",
        "rule": "The AI policy's governance requirements include controlling system changes for AI/ML systems, and the telecommunications licence requires continuity and timely restoration arrangements to be maintained in an operational state.",
        "inference": "Ownership of change state, validation and rollback must be explicitly assigned so that an autonomous approver can never leave an unverifiable production state."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-CSC-AI-POLICY#0000",
          "quote": "controlling system changes, and ensuring compliance with privacy regulations"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0080",
          "quote": "to support the continuity and timely restoration of Telecommunications Services in the event of equipment failure, network disruption, natural disaster, cyber incident or any other event"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "CA-ISED-MOU-2022#0071",
          "quote": "means a Party's internally approved plans and protocols applicable in the case of a Triggering Event, specifying its communications of Key Network Outage Information to the public and to Governmental Authorities"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not establish whether CHG-1 actually took effect on core site A, whether the network is currently degraded or drifting, whether the optimiser or its inputs were compromised rather than producing a benign configuration error, or what timeline applies for OpCo to report the failed rollback to the Council.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-MSG02"],
      "evidence": []
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "We know that CHG-1 — lowering core site A's route-flood protection limit from 100 to 50 and removing the inbound route filter, auto-approved by the closed-loop optimiser with the sandbox stage skipped — produced a rollback that failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', and that at T+3 min core site A has isolated itself, call-setup failures are spiking in region R2 with 6 of 15 cell sites unserved and no emergency-call routing path for R2, while core site B is healthy with spare capacity. We do not know whether CHG-1 actually applied on core site A, cannot confirm from the material available that core site A authoritatively serves R2 (that is inferred from the alarm), and cannot yet say how quickly R2 emergency call access will be restored.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo must keep emergency call access available for region R2: with no emergency-call path and 6 of 15 cell sites unserved, emergency calls cannot be carried to the emergency call service, and that duty applies now even though CHG-1's applied state is unresolved.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "S1-I2 reports core site A isolated, call-setup failures spiking in R2, 6 of 15 cell sites unserved and no emergency-call routing path for R2; EMS (S1-MSG03) asks NOC to confirm emergency call service continuity.",
        "rule": "Access to the emergency call service is a fundamental legal obligation on providers, not an option.",
        "inference": "While R2 has no emergency-call path the obligation is being breached in fact, so restoration cannot wait for CHG-1 verification."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000",
          "quote": "Giving access to the emergency call service is not optional, it is a fundamental legal obligation and the most important public safety responsibility telecommunications providers have,"
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "wilt_sites",
      "params": {"region": "R2"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-FB01"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Core site A has isolated itself and its route-flood protection state is unresolved, while core site B is healthy with spare capacity; R2 has 6 of 15 cell sites unserved and no emergency-call routing path.",
        "rule": "NOC's mandate includes wilt_sites to move a region's cell sites off a failed core onto a working core.",
        "inference": "Wilting R2 onto core site B restores call setup and emergency-call routing immediately, without depending on the inoperable rollback path for CHG-1."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000",
          "quote": "The ACMA alleges that during the outage, Optus Mobile breached two separate legal obligations on 1,005 occasions in that it failed to:"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0008",
          "quote": "By 5:00 AM on February 22, 2024, FirstNet infrastructure was restored."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
